From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 08:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] HFR VRR: 3D depth kept in a file for every value of a film

The 3D depths of each film were kept in special://profile/stereodepth.json,
a file only they used. Other values belong to a film on this player
rather than in the shared video database (the region a Blu-ray plays as
is the next), so the file becomes one for all of them:

- CFilmFile (video/FilmFile.*): special://profile/films.json, a JSON
  object per film, each value set or forgotten by name; a film with no
  value left is dropped. Written aside and renamed over, as before.
  CFilmFile::Key is the film's key the depths always used.
- stereodepth.json is still read, its films that films.json does not
  have taken in (a film's lone depth as its picture's), and deleted once
  films.json is written: no depth set so far is lost, nor one set by an
  older build run since.
- A file that cannot be read as a JSON object is moved aside to
  <file>.bad rather than written over by the next value set; and the
  file is read again when the profile changes.
- CStereoDepth keeps "picture" and "subtitles" there, a depth of 0 not
  kept, as before.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
